 # Changelog
 
+## 0.3.5
+
+ScrapeRight port gaps (rightkit#736), plus the cookie transfer lifted from ScrapeRight (rightkit#463). Additive. One construction-only break: `LaunchOptions` gained two public fields (`user_agent`, `extra_headers`), so code that builds it by a full struct literal without `..Default::default()` must add them; builder-style construction is unaffected. Not compiled or run yet.
+
+- `ManagedRoot` is public (rightkit#736): the managed Chrome for Testing folder (`resolve`, `at`, `path`, `current`, `previous`, `staging`, `executable`). Before, it sat in a private module, so `install::ensure_chrome_for_testing` could not be called from an app.
+- `install::ensure_default_chrome_for_testing(progress)` (feature `install`): installs the pinned build at `ManagedRoot::resolve()`, the one call an installer or updater step needs. `install::ensure_chrome_for_testing_with_progress(root, pin, progress)` reports `(DownloadKind, bytes received, bytes expected)`; `ensure_chrome_for_testing` is unchanged.
+- `BrowserPage::set_user_agent(ua, accept_language, platform)` (CDP `Emulation.setUserAgentOverride`) and `BrowserPage::set_extra_headers(&[(name, value)])` (CDP `Network.setExtraHTTPHeaders`): every request of the page carries them, no interceptor needed. Header names must be tokens, values hold no line break or NUL, and `Host`, `Content-Length`, `Transfer-Encoding` and `Connection` are refused; a repeated name keeps its last value. `LaunchOptions::user_agent(..)` and `LaunchOptions::extra_header(name, value)` apply the same to every page the session opens, before its first navigation (`new_page`, `new_page_with`); validated at launch. Pages a site opens itself are not covered.
+- Cookies: `CookieRecord`, `to_netscape` / `parse_netscape` (`#HttpOnly_` prefix, session expiry 0, fields with a tab or line break skipped, empty values kept), `BrowserPage::cookies`, `set_cookies`, `export_cookies_netscape(domains)` and `import_cookies_netscape`. These do not pass through the admission hook (no new `ActionKind`, so the public enum is unchanged); the caller decides which cookies may leave the session.
+- yt-dlp mapping: `cookie_keyword_for_executable(path)`, `BrowserKind::cookies_from_browser_keyword()` and `cookies_from_browser_spec(keyword, profile_dir)`.
+- Browser lookup: on Windows `browser_executable(kind)` and `find_chrome` also try the per-user `%LOCALAPPDATA%` install (Chrome, Chromium, Edge, Brave) after `%ProgramFiles%` and `%ProgramFiles(x86)%`, which are now read from the environment (fixed `C:\Program Files` paths when unset). `browser_executable(BrowserKind::Brave)` therefore finds a per-user Brave; on Linux it also checks `brave-browser-stable`, `brave` and the snap paths, on macOS `~/Applications`.
+- `launch_visible_and_wait(VisibleLaunch, timeout)`, `VisibleBrowser` (`launch`, `wait`, `terminate`, `pid`) and `VisibleOutcome { Exited { code }, TimedOut }`: a plain visible browser on a dedicated profile directory with no DevTools connection, waited on until the user closes it, for sign-in flows. The URL must be http(s) or `about:blank`; the flags that open a debugging endpoint or redirect the profile are refused; a real browser profile is refused. The process tree is owned and ends on timeout, `terminate` or drop.
+
 ## 0.3.4 (2026-10-17)
 
 - Doc fix (rightkit#267): the `PINNED_CHROME_FOR_TESTING` comment no longer says every digest is `Sha256Pin::Todo`; the 155.0.8059.39 table carries recorded digests for mac-arm64, mac-x64, linux64 and win64 (plus the win64 headless shell). `Sha256Pin::Todo` still refuses a download.
